\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Worship and thanks, and lessing,
\par And strength ascribe to Jesus!
\par Jesus alone
\par Defends His own,
\par When earth and hell oppress us.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Jesus with joy we witness
\par Almighty to deliver;
\par Our seals set to,
\par That God is true,
\par And reigns a King for ever.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Omnipotent Redeemer,
\par Our ransomed souls adore Thee:
\par Our Saviour Thou,
\par We find it now,
\par And give  Thee all the glory.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par We sing Thine arm unshortened,
\par Brought through our sore temptation;
\par With heart and voice
\par In Thee rejoice,
\par The God of our salvation.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thine arm hath safely brought us
\par A way no more expected,
\par Than when Thy sheep
\par Passed through the deep,
\par By crystal walls protected.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par The glory was our rearward,
\par Thine hand our lives did cover,
\par And we, even we,
\par Have passed the sea,
\par And marched triumphant over.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The world and Satan's malice
\par Thou, Jesus, hast confounded;
\par And, by Thy grace,
\par With songs of praise
\par Our happy souls resounded.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Accepting our deliverance,
\par We triumph in Thy favour,
\par And for the love
\par Which now we prove
\par Shall praise Thy name for ever.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

